  What's on screen

  Left column — 8 sliders, grouped so related assumptions sit together:

  ┌──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┬───────────────┐
  │          Growth          │       Profitability       │ Discount rate │
  ├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼───────────────┤
  │ Year 1 growth (−20–100%) │ Gross margin (0–100%)     │ WACC (4–20%)  │
  ├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼───────────────┤
  │ Year 5 growth (−10–60%)  │ Opex % of revenue (0–60%) │               │
  ├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼───────────────┤
  │ Terminal growth (0–6%)   │ Tax rate (0–40%)          │               │
  ├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼───────────────┤
  │ Forecast years (5–20)    │                           │               │
  └──────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┴───────────────┘

  Growth ranges go negative so you can model a downturn, not just varying
  degrees of good news.

  Right column — four KPI cards (intrinsic value/share, upside/downside, signal,
  enterprise value) over a valuation bridge that walks PV of forecast → PV of
  terminal → EV → +cash → −debt → ÷shares → per-share value. Every card
  recomputes on drag, no submit button.

  The signal uses ±15% bands: BUY above +15%, SELL below −15%, HOLD between.
  Those thresholds are BUY_ABOVE/SELL_BELOW at the top of app.py if you want
  different cutoffs.

