  A real bug the work surfaced

  My mode-equivalence test failed, and it was right to. Year-2 operating margin
  rendered as 60.6% in taper mode but 60.5% in per-year mode — same forecast,
  different displayed number.

  Cause: the taper computes 0.6055; the per-year path computes 60.55/100 = 
  0.6054999999999999. Identical to the arithmetic, but they straddle a rounding
  boundary at one decimal place. It was invisible until this table started
  displaying all ten years. Fixed by normalising both paths in dcf.py (_clean,
  rounding to 10dp — far finer than any real assumption), not by loosening the
  test.

