     Surface the DCF engine's year-by-year workings

     Context

     The model already computes a full forecast, but the Valuation tab shows
     almost none of
     it. YearRow carries revenue, free_cash_flow, discount_factor and pv_of_fcf
     for
     every year, and only Year 1 is ever displayed. A reader sees the inputs and
     the final
     per-share number with the ten years in between hidden — which is exactly
     the part that
     makes a DCF checkable.

     Audit of the four requested steps against the current code:

     ┌────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │            Step            │                   Status                   │
     ├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ 1. Projected revenue +     │                                            │
     │ undiscounted FCF in        │ Computed already; not displayed            │
     │ results, shown in the      │                                            │
     │ table                      │                                            │
     ├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │                            │ Already exact — dcf.py:199 is final_fcf *  │
     │ 2. Terminal value uses     │ (1 + terminal_growth) / (wacc -            │
     │ Gordon Growth              │ terminal_growth). No change; pin it with a │
     │                            │  test                                      │
     ├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ 3. Discounted FCF and PV   │ Computed already; per-year PV not          │
     │ of terminal value shown    │ displayed, aggregates are                  │
     ├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ 4. Subtract net debt,      │ Already done — bridge runs + Cash → − Debt │
     │ divide by shares, display  │  → ÷ Shares. Only the wording lacks an     │
     │ per share                  │ explicit net-debt line                     │
     └────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘

     So this is one new table plus two small presentational additions, not an
