       current look.

     Bridge gains one row: = Net debt between the cash/debt pair and equity
     value, rendered
     in parentheses when negative (NVIDIA holds net cash, so it reads (34.7)).

     Note on the 9 columns: NOPAT minus FCF is net capex plus ΔWorking capital,
     so those
     two drivers are implied rather than shown. Adding them makes it 11 columns
     and fully
     traceable — say the word and I will.

     Changes — dcf.py

     Add a net_debt property to DCFResult (debt - cash) so the UI does not
     recompute it.
     No change to any calculation: the engine already does everything steps 1-4
