  Defensible: WACC — that is where the research effort belongs.

  How it avoids false precision

  Two readings, reported rather than blended. The weighted mean says HOLD
  (+4.7%); the probability mass says SELL (25% above price). Blending them would
  hide the conflict, and the conflict is the most informative thing here. On
  disagreement it takes the more cautious verdict, forces conviction to low, and
  names the case responsible.

  Conviction tracks the range, and it moves correctly:

  cut  25/75  (mixed)      SELL / low       ⚠ warning shown
  cut   0/0   (all bull)   BUY  / high      no warning, no straddle
  cut 100/100 (all bear)   SELL / high
  cut   5/30  (bull-heavy) BUY  / moderate

  Headline range rounds to the nearest $10 — a range $400 wide doesn't support
  cents. Exact figures stay in the table below.

  Verification

  Every rendered break-even value round-trips through run_dcf to exactly 
  $180.00. That's the test that matters: a drifting solver would still print
  plausible required values and build a confident verdict on them.

  Three corrections to my own plan

