  Two tiers

  Blocking → red card on every panel, and in scenario mode the case drops out
  with its probability mass reported:
  - WACC ≤ terminal growth (existing)
  - terminal multiple > 100× (new)
  - shares ≤ 0 (existing)

  I guarded the multiple, not the spread, because a 1pp spread is harmless at a
  20% WACC and ruinous at 4% — a spread rule would block sane inputs and pass
  mad ones. The message names the multiple, which is the figure an analyst
  recognises.

  Warning → valued, with an amber notice above the numbers:
  - multiple > 40× · negative final-year FCF · terminal growth > 4% · operating
    margin > 75% · WACC < 7%

  Those last three reuse MAX_TERMINAL_GROWTH, NVDA_GROSS_MARGIN and
  MIN_CREDIBLE_WACC — the constants already driving the break-even verdicts. One
  definition of "implausible", not two that drift. A test asserts they stay
  tied.

  Warnings carry a code as well as prose, so tests key off behaviour rather than
  wording, and a flagged case gets a ⚠ marker on its row in the scenario table
  — visible without opening the tab.

  The thing I was most careful about

  The defaults trip nothing. Left pane and Base 14.7×, Bear 10.2×, Bull 20.8×,
  margins 62–65% against 75%, positive FCF throughout. Bull's terminal growth
  sits exactly at 4% and every threshold tests strictly, so it stays clean.
  There's a dedicated test for this — a validation layer that fires on the
  opening screen just teaches people to ignore it.

  A collision worth knowing about

  The break-even solver brackets WACC from 4.01%, which at 3% terminal growth is
  a 102× multiple — the new block rejects it, the solver would see a nan at the
  bracket end, and the entire WACC break-even row would have silently reported
  "unreachable". I moved the bracket to 5% (51.5×) and added a test that the row
  still solves and still round-trips to $180.00.

  The sensitivity grids also improved: at WACC 4% two of nine rows now render –
  instead of four-figure values per share.

  Valid numbers are untouched — 133.70 / 188.85 / 63+63 cells / Base 133.70 · 
  Bear 38.48 · Bull 449.49.

  The amber notice is new markup nobody has seen; it inherits the colour
  treatment from the recommendation's existing warning, which lowers the risk
  without removing it.

