     Re-base the model on the NVIDIA Exhibits

     Context

     NVIDIA_Exhibits.xlsx was compiled 30 July 2026. The model was built on
     FY2025.
     It is a full fiscal year stale, and the gap is not cosmetic — revenue has
     since risen 65%,
     the cash pile has more than doubled, and the share price has moved. Nearly
     every default is
     now wrong, and three of them were flagged in the README as unverified
     judgment when the
     exhibit in fact supplies a sourced figure.

     The stale defaults also make the app say the wrong thing. Today it opens at
     $133.70,
     −25.7%, SELL — a confident bearish call resting on year-old revenue.
     Rebuilt on the
     exhibit it opens at $194.91, +2.6%, and the probability-weighted view is
     $199.90, +5.2%, HOLD at low conviction. That is a much more interesting and
     more
     honest starting point: the market is priced roughly for consensus, and the
     entire argument
     is about the shape of the deceleration curve.

     The three judgment calls you settled:

