  Two things I found while reconciling

  Year-1 margin should be 65.6%, not FY2026's 60.4%. FY2026's gross margin
  dipped to 71.1% from 75.0% — a one-off. Q1 FY2027 came back at 74.9% gross /
  65.6% operating, and Q2 guidance implies 65.6% again. Using the full-year
  figure would have carried that one-off through all ten forecast years.

  Working capital is now solved for rather than quoted. This was the one default
  the README admitted was a guess. Exhibit 5's "19.3%" is computed on a
  different basis than the model uses, so I solved for the figure that
